§ CSLv3 AGENT REASONING SUBSTRATE
I> token↓ per step → step-count↑ per budget → depth↑
I> CoT in CSL = denser → same context window = more reasoning steps
I> reconciled: pasted (§P/§D/§T/§S/§C structured blocks), specs/ (§9 simpler)
I> v3 adopts structured think-blocks (richer) + compression evidence (both)

§ THOUGHT-BLOCK GRAMMAR
  W! all agent reasoning uses this structure inside <think> tags

<think>
§ P (PROBLEM)
  given: ⟨facts⟩
  goal:  G

§ D (DECOMPOSITION)
  G → [sub₁, sub₂, ...]

§ T (TRACE)
  sub₁ ~> approach_a ✓ → partial₁
  sub₂ ~> approach_b ✗ ∵ ⟨reason⟩
        → retry(approach_c) ✓ → partial₂

§ S (SYNTHESIS)
  partial₁ ⊕ partial₂ ⇒ answer :T

§ C (CHECK)
  answer ⊨ G? ✓
  edge: ⟨case⟩ → handles? ✓
∎
</think>

§ REASONING GLYPHS (§01 extension)
  ?!      → surprising / counterintuitive
  !?      → suspect / needs-verify
  ⟲       → iterate / loop back
  ⤓       → dive deeper
  ⤒       → lift / abstract up
  ⟐       → pivot / reframe
  ⚠       → pitfall / common-error
  ★       → key insight
  ✎       → note-to-self

§ BELIEF CALCULUS
  p₀.₉    → probability 0.9
  p↑      → increasing confidence
  p↓      → decreasing confidence
  p⊥      → contradictory evidence → W! resolve before proceeding

§ DENSE TRACE EXAMPLE
<think>
§ P
  voxel engine stutter @ chunk boundary
  hw: Intel 12-14gen + Arc A770
§ D
  stutter → [mesh.regen, alloc.spike, gpu.stall]
§ T
  mesh.regen ~> profile → 2ms ✓ ¬culprit
  alloc.spike ~> heap-trace → 47MB burst ?!
    ⤓ source = chunk-LOD-promote ✓ found
  gpu.stall ~> pipeline-stats → idle 0 ✓ clean
§ S
  culprit = alloc.spike ∵ LOD-promote allocates fresh
  fix → pool.LOD-buffers + ring.allocator
§ C
  ✓ eliminates 47MB spike
  ⚠ edge: extreme LOD jumps → pool-overflow? → cap+fallback
∎
</think>

§ COMPRESSION EVIDENCE
  EN reasoning: ~45 tokens (typical 5-step chain)
  CSLv3 reasoning: ~18 tokens (same chain)
  ratio: 2.5× (reasoning compresses less than spec ∵ less structural regularity)
  
  EN spec: ~200 tokens (constraint block)
  CSLv3 spec: ~40 tokens
  ratio: 5× (specs compress well ∵ high structural regularity)

§ DRIFT MITIGATION
  ⚠ agent-drift: LLM may translate-back to EN internally
  mitigation:
    W! system-prompt: "reason in CSL"
    W! reinforce via §P/§D/§T/§S/§C structure
    R! when reasoning block > 10 lines → check for EN drift
    R! if EN drift detected → ⟐ pivot back to CSL glyphs

§ CSLv3 REASONING vs EN REASONING
I> from v2 specs/ §9.2:
  Q? arch → hot-reload?
    arch = ECS + archetype-storage
    hot-reload needs: serialize → reload-module → deserialize
    archetype-storage ⇒ contiguous-memory ⇒ serialize=easy
    ✓ arch → hot-reload supported
  
  EN equivalent (45 tokens):
  "I need to figure out whether this architecture supports hot-reloading.
   The system uses component-based design with ECS. Components stored in
   archetypes. Hot-reloading requires serializing state, reloading module,
   then deserializing. Archetype storage makes serialization easy because
   contiguous memory. Therefore yes, supports hot-reloading."
  
  CSLv3: 18 tokens. same semantic content. 2.5× compression.
∎
